<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŏchaeus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροχαῖος</span> (cf.
				<i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 9, § 988</span></i>).
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A metrical foot of two syllables</i>, <i>a long and a short</i> (— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">˘),</span>”
				<i>a trochee</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 47, 182</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 80</span></i>; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 8 praef.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another name for the</i> tribrachys, <i>a metrical foot of three short syllables</i>
			(˘ 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">˘ ˘),</span>”
				<i>a tribrach</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 57, 193</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 82</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
